# Overleaf honours a latexmkrc in the project root, and this one exists for the free
# plan's compile timeout. A clean build of this template needs three XeLaTeX passes plus
# biber, which does not fit; a single pass does.
#
# So each compile is one pass. Cross-references and citations converge across successive
# compiles instead of within one: the first compile after a structural edit may leave a
# "??" or two, the second resolves them. The bibliography is shipped precompiled as
# main-report.bbl so biber only runs when that file is missing.
#
# Do not use this for the final submission build. Delete it (or build locally with plain
# `latexmk -xelatex main-report.tex`) so everything resolves in one go.

$max_repeat = 1;        # one XeLaTeX pass per compile
$bibtex_use = 1.5;      # run biber only if main-report.bbl is missing
$force_mode = 1;        # still produce the PDF when a reference is not yet resolved
